'''Hurricane Nadira''' was a major [[Capuyaquiran Sea]] hurricane in 2019 that affected the [[Bolodun and Kuvari Islands]] and [[Guajicutea]], with the equivalent of {{W|Saffir–Simpson scale#Category 4|Category 4}}-force sustained winds at peak intensity.

== Impact ==

In the [[Bolodun and Kuvari Islands]], Hurricane Nadira caused moderate damage in the capital [[Ominira]]. The city's raised, hurricane-resistant construction, adopted after [[Hurricane Sahan]] in 1969, limited the impact compared with the earlier disaster.

The storm also struck Guajicutea, damaging many port facilities, especially in [[Waribá]], and hitting tourism hard across the region as port access, cruise turnover, and waterfront services slowed at once. Hotels and transport operators lost revenue, and construction and repair work was redirected to recovery.

